From e537cb9a999137cb3426386657fa868d7ea83ec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Creasy <5614134+jcrben@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:19:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] coredump/launcher: retry resolving KCrash metadata instead of
 a single check

drkonqi-coredump-launcher is woken up independently, via the coredump
socket, of KCrash's own in-process signal handler writing the sidecar
kcrash-metadata/<exe>.<bootid>.<pid>.ini file. The two race: the launcher
previously checked for that file exactly once and, on a miss, permanently
fell back to synthesized/generic metadata and logged "KCrash metadata not
marked complete" - even though the file is written completely and
correctly (including the KCrashComplete marker) a short moment later.

Confirmed with gdb on a live crash: the file is opened O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|
O_TRUNC by KCrash's handler and, once written, is fully valid - the
launcher's single check had simply already run and given up before that
write landed.

Poll for the file for a bounded 2s window (checking every 50ms) instead of
giving up on the first miss. Added an autotest that reproduces the race
with a delayed write and verifies both that the fix waits for it and that
a genuinely-never-written file still resolves promptly to empty.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GRSmqLcEvFEEPJBtTtMeCc
